Key things to understand:

MiDaS returns relative/inverse depth — higher values mean closer to the camera. There's no unit. To map it to real meters you need to calibrate by placing an object at a known distance (say 1m) and recording its depth value, then computing a scale factor K. The formula K / depth gives an approximate metric estimate.

